::cue(c.colora8c7fa) { color: #a8c7fa; }
::cue(c.credits) { color: #a8c7fa; font-size: 78%; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Premium</c></b>
Keep the project alive: <c.colora8c7fa>ko-fi.com/not6ip</c>

2
00:00:25.370 --> 00:00:30.620
Every time I look up to the sky after the rain

3
00:00:30.620 --> 00:00:36.130
I think back to when I was a crybaby

4
00:00:36.130 --> 00:00:43.870
I was chasing somebody's back blindly

5
00:00:43.940 --> 00:00:46.850
Thinking "I want to be stronger"

6
00:00:46.850 --> 00:00:52.030
The word "thank you" has faded into the wind now

7
00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:57.210
Am I getting stronger?

8
00:00:57.410 --> 00:01:02.880
I don't know the answer yet

9
00:01:03.010 --> 00:01:08.400
That's why I'll keep walking ahead

10
00:01:08.550 --> 00:01:11.030
So let's go

11
00:01:11.030 --> 00:01:14.240
Without stopping

12
00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:19.480
Without giving up to the flow of time

13
00:01:19.480 --> 00:01:25.090
I'll keep getting back up

14
00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:30.730
Because I don't want to lose something precious

15
00:01:30.740 --> 00:01:35.850
The voice inside of me

16
00:01:35.860 --> 00:01:41.250
keeps sustaining me

17
00:01:41.250 --> 00:01:46.380
Wicked rain will get in my way

18
00:01:46.390 --> 00:01:51.320
But I won't walk away

19
00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:56.780
So let's go

20
00:01:56.780 --> 00:02:00.060
Without stopping

21
00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:05.350
Without giving up to the flow of time

22
00:02:05.360 --> 00:02:10.990
I'll keep getting back up

23
00:02:10.990 --> 00:02:16.350
Because I don't want to lose something precious

24
00:02:16.360 --> 00:02:22.050
To the future I believe in...

25
00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:42.420
<b>Navy Headquarters</b>

26
00:02:55.090 --> 00:02:58.920
It looks like you barely managed to hold on to your lives.

27
00:02:59.020 --> 00:03:02.080
If I hadn't shown up with the antidote...

28
00:02:59.610 --> 00:03:04.650
<b>Impel Down</b>

29
00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:05.440
you'd all be dead by now.

30
00:03:05.440 --> 00:03:07.430
You underestimated Magellan.

31
00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:11.430
We're still alive!

32
00:03:11.430 --> 00:03:16.450
You were... destined to come here.

33
00:03:18.710 --> 00:03:22.100
Well, I really thought we were going to die.

34
00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:24.600
Seems like we...

35
00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:26.890
got lucky this time.

36
00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:34.250
Heaven chooses who survives,

37
00:03:34.250 --> 00:03:36.920
but if you give up, you've already lost!

38
00:03:39.880 --> 00:03:42.570
Might as well live in the moment.

39
00:03:43.330 --> 00:03:44.790
Hey, Shiryu!

40
00:03:57.160 --> 00:04:01.290
It was nice of you to save us. Thanks a lot.

41
00:04:01.290 --> 00:04:03.610
I welcome you once again.

42
00:04:03.610 --> 00:04:05.660
You'll make a fine addition to our crew!

43
00:04:05.660 --> 00:04:09.180
I have no future here.

44
00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:12.760
I was hoping to meet a man like you.

45
00:04:21.020 --> 00:04:25.490
<b>The World Government's Private Route: The Tarai Current</b>

46
00:04:24.720 --> 00:04:27.490
Let vus rest Inazuma here.

47
00:04:27.490 --> 00:04:31.060
Huh? You mean the poison has affected him that badly?

48
00:04:31.060 --> 00:04:34.550
Vi was able to treat the poison he hit vme with,

49
00:04:35.300 --> 00:04:38.660
using vmy Healing and Tension Hormones...

50
00:04:44.360 --> 00:04:50.470
But that technique has some nasty side effects.
 It can even shorten your lifespan.

51
00:04:50.780 --> 00:04:55.970
It'd be better for him to recuperate naturally.

52
00:04:56.500 --> 00:05:00.450
Once vyour lifespan has been shortened, vyou'll never be able to reclaim the years vyou've lost.

53
00:05:00.450 --> 00:05:03.920
Inazuma is an important newkama to the Revolutionary Army.

54
00:05:04.290 --> 00:05:08.720
He shouldn't overexert himself now.

55
00:05:17.310 --> 00:05:20.670
You know, he wasn't such a bad guy, after all.

56
00:05:22.050 --> 00:05:24.330
We just reunited,

57
00:05:24.330 --> 00:05:26.800
and he's gone and saved me again!

58
00:05:31.580 --> 00:05:32.900
Bon-chan!

59
00:05:32.900 --> 00:05:33.800
Brother Bon!

60
00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:38.520
Bon-chan!

61
00:05:39.850 --> 00:05:44.130
Hey, how long're you guys
 gonna stand 'round sobbin' for?

62
00:05:44.770 --> 00:05:47.810
He was a good guy but he's dead now.

63
00:05:47.810 --> 00:05:50.490
Let's just celebrate!

64
00:05:50.880 --> 00:05:52.630
Celebrate our freedom!

65
00:05:55.180 --> 00:05:58.720
Or, if you'd like, we could make it a wake for Mr. 2.

66
00:06:02.680 --> 00:06:05.360
What a bloody nice service!

67
00:06:06.650 --> 00:06:11.150
Bon-chan could still be alive, big-nose!

68
00:06:11.150 --> 00:06:13.530
Who're you callin' big-nose?!

69
00:06:13.530 --> 00:06:17.040
You, you red-nosed, round-nosed, stupid-nosed idiot!

70
00:06:17.040 --> 00:06:21.260
Well, you've got a rubbery, stretchy, stupid face!

71
00:06:21.260 --> 00:06:22.750
What'd you say?!

72
00:06:23.480 --> 00:06:26.300
Oh, just do whatever the hell you want.

73
00:06:31.840 --> 00:06:39.860
I thought only Merfolk were able to talk to fish.

74
00:06:39.860 --> 00:06:42.980
I'm surprised you were able to summon whale sharks.

75
00:06:42.980 --> 00:06:46.820
What's odd about a fishman being on
good terms with sea creatures?

76
00:06:47.540 --> 00:06:50.240
It's just odd.

77
00:06:50.240 --> 00:06:52.290
I mean, for such a savage race...

78
00:06:53.340 --> 00:06:55.820
I suppose you're an exception.

79
00:06:55.820 --> 00:06:59.090
Well, I'll take that as a compliment.

80
00:06:59.940 --> 00:07:03.170
I can't deny that Fishmen are savage.

81
00:07:03.460 --> 00:07:05.250
Bon-chan isn't dead!

82
00:07:07.460 --> 00:07:09.940
Captain Buggy got a second red nose!

83
00:07:12.660 --> 00:07:14.510
Luffy-kun.

84
00:07:14.840 --> 00:07:20.090
Thanks to you, I have a chance to help with rescuing Ace-san.

85
00:07:21.080 --> 00:07:23.000
I'm indebted to you.

86
00:07:23.000 --> 00:07:25.260
Oh, don't mention it.

87
00:07:26.600 --> 00:07:30.760
Besides, I'm glad you're with us. You're really strong!

88
00:07:31.160 --> 00:07:38.100
This isn't the first time I've been indebted to you.

89
00:07:38.100 --> 00:07:40.600
I should express my gratitude and apologies but...

90
00:07:40.600 --> 00:07:43.410
we must focus on our current objective.

91
00:07:44.100 --> 00:07:47.190
You can call me Jinbe!

92
00:07:47.190 --> 00:07:52.480
I used to be one of the Seven Warlords, but I've abandoned that title!

93
00:07:52.480 --> 00:07:56.240
Let's unleash hell at Navy HQ!

94
00:07:57.240 --> 00:08:03.000
We must save Ace-san,
 so that Okama-kun's efforts won't go to waste!

95
00:08:03.280 --> 00:08:04.620
A warlord?

96
00:08:04.620 --> 00:08:06.800
Navy HQ?

97
00:08:06.800 --> 00:08:08.970
Huh?!

98
00:08:08.970 --> 00:08:12.540
Hey, hey, hey! You were one of the Seven Warlords?!

99
00:08:12.540 --> 00:08:14.540
No wonder you're so strong!

100
00:08:17.400 --> 00:08:20.620
Forgive me. I should have introduced myself sooner.

101
00:08:20.620 --> 00:08:22.560
It's surprising you didn't know...

102
00:08:22.560 --> 00:08:26.390
Hey! What do you mean, “Navy HQ”?!

103
00:08:26.390 --> 00:08:30.720
You better not be saying that this ship is heading for Navy HQ!

104
00:08:30.720 --> 00:08:35.560
You know about the war between
 the Navy and the Whitebeard Pirates, right?!

105
00:08:36.250 --> 00:08:37.530
Uh, what?

106
00:08:37.530 --> 00:08:38.540
Navy HQ?

107
00:08:38.540 --> 00:08:43.020
What are you saying?
 It's not our fault that you're so dim-witted.

108
00:08:43.020 --> 00:08:44.070
What?!

109
00:08:44.070 --> 00:08:50.820
Now that we're through the Gates of Justice, the only possible destinations are Enies Lobby and Navy HQ.

110
00:08:49.690 --> 00:08:54.360
<b>Mary Geoise</b>
<b>Enies Lobby</b>
<b>Navy Headquarters
(Marineford)</b>
<b>The Great Prison
Impel Down</b>

111
00:08:50.820 --> 00:08:54.650
We're currently traveling the government's exclusive route, the Tarai Current.

112
00:08:54.650 --> 00:08:58.440
This is an enormous vortex that connects the government's three main facilities.

113
00:08:58.440 --> 00:09:04.070
The only reason we escaped in the first place was because we wanted to join the battle.

114
00:09:04.920 --> 00:09:08.320
Yeah, the real fight starts now!

115
00:09:08.320 --> 00:09:11.160
“The real fight starts now?!”

116
00:09:11.160 --> 00:09:14.120
N-Nobody told us about this!

117
00:09:14.120 --> 00:09:16.760
Stop the ship right now, damn you!

118
00:09:16.760 --> 00:09:18.000
Stop it!

119
00:09:18.000 --> 00:09:22.000
We're already riding the current.
There's no way for me to stop it!

120
00:09:22.000 --> 00:09:24.300
Why don't you two just get off?

121
00:09:24.300 --> 00:09:27.650
-Ok, goodbye!
-Bye!

122
00:09:27.650 --> 00:09:32.480
You really think we'll get off?!
 We're both devil fruit users! We'd drown!

123
00:09:32.480 --> 00:09:39.620
The Navy high command and the Warlords versus the Whitebeard Pirates... this war is scary as hell!

124
00:09:50.950 --> 00:09:55.210
If that's where we're going, I'd rather go back to prison!

125
00:09:56.540 --> 00:09:58.710
All of us from 'Kama Land knew about this.

126
00:10:05.580 --> 00:10:09.490
Hey, can you hear something?

127
00:10:30.640 --> 00:10:33.150
M-Maybe we should pretend we're not here?

128
00:10:36.220 --> 00:10:37.530
Uh, hello?

129
00:10:37.530 --> 00:10:39.020
He answered!

130
00:10:39.020 --> 00:10:41.020
This is Navy HQ.

131
00:10:41.020 --> 00:10:42.750
Yeah, this is Luffy.

132
00:10:42.750 --> 00:10:44.520
Don't tell him your name! You're a pirate!

133
00:10:44.520 --> 00:10:52.460
We received word from Impel Down security
 that a group of escapees commandeered a ship.

134
00:10:53.010 --> 00:10:57.160
Judging from the information we received before we lost contact with Impel Down,

135
00:10:57.160 --> 00:11:00.510
we've determined that there are two ringleaders behind this breakout.

136
00:11:01.670 --> 00:11:02.640
Two?

137
00:11:02.640 --> 00:11:05.330
The pirate Straw Hat Luffy,

138
00:11:06.130 --> 00:11:08.000
and his fellow pirate...

139
00:11:08.000 --> 00:11:09.510
Buggy the Clown.

140
00:11:11.630 --> 00:11:13.660
-Huh?!
-W-What?!

141
00:11:13.660 --> 00:11:14.560
Seriously?!

142
00:11:14.560 --> 00:11:18.320
They're treating Captain Buggy as a bigger threat than the warlords?!

143
00:11:18.320 --> 00:11:20.820
Who are you?!

144
00:11:21.370 --> 00:11:23.130
Why me?

145
00:11:23.650 --> 00:11:24.990
Hand me the papers.

146
00:11:24.990 --> 00:11:26.570
Yes, sir. Here they are.

147
00:11:26.570 --> 00:11:30.480
We've underestimated you in the past. 
We assumed you were just some upstart pirate.

148
00:11:30.480 --> 00:11:33.540
Buggy the Clown, we never would have guessed

149
00:11:33.540 --> 00:11:38.490
that you were a former crewmate of the pirate king, Gold Roger.

150
00:11:39.090 --> 00:11:40.680
How'd they find out?!

151
00:11:42.310 --> 00:11:44.470
You were on the Oro Jackson?!

152
00:11:44.470 --> 00:11:45.710
This is huge!

153
00:11:45.710 --> 00:11:48.510
A-A star! He's a pirate star!

154
00:11:48.510 --> 00:11:54.910
We've also received word that you are like a brother to Red-Haired Shanks of the Four Emperors.

155
00:11:54.910 --> 00:11:56.490
What did you say?!

156
00:11:56.490 --> 00:12:03.230
I'm impressed that a man of your caliber was able to lie low until now.

157
00:12:03.230 --> 00:12:05.870
We won't underestimate you,
 now that you've come this far.

158
00:12:07.310 --> 00:12:08.570
Uh, no...

159
00:12:08.570 --> 00:12:12.030
We've yet to find any connection between you and Fire Fist Ace...

160
00:12:12.030 --> 00:12:17.370
but I'm sure your objective is the same as Straw Hat Luffy's: to save Ace.

161
00:12:17.370 --> 00:12:22.250
We've also confirmed that Jinbe, Crocodile, Ivankov,

162
00:12:22.250 --> 00:12:27.540
as well as over 200 other escapees, are on board the ship.

163
00:12:27.540 --> 00:12:29.360
I'm warning you all now...

164
00:12:29.980 --> 00:12:35.450
Unless we open the Gates of Justice,
 you will not be able to reach Marineford,

165
00:12:35.450 --> 00:12:39.040
nor will you be able to escape from the Tarai Current.

166
00:12:39.040 --> 00:12:43.610
None of you have any chance of escape.

167
00:12:45.130 --> 00:12:47.240
You'd better resign yourselves to that.

168
00:12:47.240 --> 00:12:48.100
That is all.

169
00:12:48.100 --> 00:12:49.440
Hey, wait, Navy!

170
00:12:53.250 --> 00:12:55.620
I'm definitely going to save Ace!

171
00:12:57.150 --> 00:12:59.460
I'll put your potatoes on a platter!

172
00:13:00.650 --> 00:13:01.930
Potatoes...?

173
00:13:07.280 --> 00:13:09.950
“Heads!” It's “heads on a platter,” Straw Hat-san!

174
00:13:09.950 --> 00:13:13.190
Like this is any time to be preparing potatoes!

175
00:13:13.650 --> 00:13:17.720
Hey, why is this guy picking a fight with Navy HQ anyway?

176
00:13:17.720 --> 00:13:20.410
No, wait! More importantly, Captain Buggy,

177
00:13:20.410 --> 00:13:23.100
you were a member of the pirate king's crew?!

178
00:13:23.100 --> 00:13:25.650
And you're also like a brother to Red Hair?!

179
00:13:25.650 --> 00:13:30.400
Our savior is truly one amazing pirate!

180
00:13:30.400 --> 00:13:31.270
No, wait!

181
00:13:31.810 --> 00:13:36.650
Oh, crap! Now that they know,
 the government will start hunting me!

182
00:13:36.650 --> 00:13:39.260
Well, I never expected him to have that kind of past.

183
00:13:39.260 --> 00:13:41.280
And despite that, he's so weak.

184
00:13:43.160 --> 00:13:46.120
But then, how can he be such a coward?

185
00:13:46.120 --> 00:13:49.460
There's at least one black sheep on every ship.

186
00:13:51.280 --> 00:13:52.840
Shut up!

187
00:13:52.840 --> 00:13:55.380
Now that you mention it...

188
00:13:55.800 --> 00:13:59.510
If you're from the East Blue, then maybe you know a pirate named Buggy as well?

189
00:13:59.950 --> 00:14:03.190
That old first mate guy mentioned something about this, too.

190
00:14:03.470 --> 00:14:05.350
Huh? The first mate?

191
00:14:06.360 --> 00:14:09.520
An old guy named Rayleigh. You know him, right?

192
00:14:09.520 --> 00:14:13.170
What?! You met Rayleigh-san?!

193
00:14:13.170 --> 00:14:15.670
Oh, that takes me back! The first mate, huh?

194
00:14:15.670 --> 00:14:16.530
Where'd you meet him?

195
00:14:16.530 --> 00:14:18.990
Dark King Rayleigh's name came up!

196
00:14:18.990 --> 00:14:20.490
What an incredible conversation!

197
00:14:21.410 --> 00:14:26.080
Captain Buggy! You truly are a dangerous man!

198
00:14:26.080 --> 00:14:27.210
No, no!

199
00:14:27.210 --> 00:14:28.810
Wait a second!

200
00:14:28.810 --> 00:14:30.820
I mean, that's true and all,

201
00:14:30.820 --> 00:14:33.250
but compared to those big shots,

202
00:14:33.250 --> 00:14:35.520
the life I've led up till now is just...

203
00:14:35.520 --> 00:14:39.670
You're amazing! You were a member of that legendary pirate crew!

204
00:14:39.670 --> 00:14:42.010
Buggy! Buggy!

205
00:14:42.010 --> 00:14:43.930
You idiots!

206
00:14:45.260 --> 00:14:48.730
Quit cheering! I was technically just an apprentice!

207
00:14:48.730 --> 00:14:52.840
You may be grateful to me for freeing you, but...

208
00:14:52.840 --> 00:14:56.320
No, I'm telling you, you've got it wrong!

209
00:14:57.010 --> 00:15:00.190
Well, not all of it is wrong.

210
00:15:00.190 --> 00:15:02.050
Right! Wait a second...

211
00:15:02.050 --> 00:15:07.130
It's true that the Navy has 
overestimated me, but this could be a good thing!

212
00:15:07.130 --> 00:15:10.830
That's right! Nothing they said was a lie!

213
00:15:10.830 --> 00:15:13.960
There's no doubt that my reputation has grown!

214
00:15:13.960 --> 00:15:16.170
If, by chance, someone...

215
00:15:16.170 --> 00:15:17.460
like me...

216
00:15:18.920 --> 00:15:23.890
manages to kill Whitebeard today, then I could become one of...

217
00:15:23.890 --> 00:15:25.220
the Four Emperors?!

218
00:15:25.220 --> 00:15:27.720
No, no, no, more than that...

219
00:15:28.680 --> 00:15:31.480
I could become king of the pirates!

220
00:15:31.480 --> 00:15:36.670
That's right! These escapees all have higher bounties than me!

221
00:15:36.670 --> 00:15:38.900
I could put them to good use!

222
00:15:42.110 --> 00:15:43.150
I can do it!

223
00:15:43.150 --> 00:15:47.890
Captain Buggy! We will follow you wherever you go!

224
00:15:49.580 --> 00:15:54.500
Just give the order! We'll steal the ship from the guys who wanna go to Navy HQ!

225
00:15:54.500 --> 00:15:57.300
And then we'll be free!

226
00:15:57.890 --> 00:16:00.070
Now, Straw Hat...

227
00:16:00.070 --> 00:16:02.310
how about handing this ship over to us?!

228
00:16:02.310 --> 00:16:06.240
We finally escaped! You think we'll go to Navy HQ?!

229
00:16:06.240 --> 00:16:09.850
We've got Captain Buggy on our side!

230
00:16:09.850 --> 00:16:11.990
We're counting on ya, Captain Buggy!

231
00:16:13.230 --> 00:16:25.950
Buggy! Buggy!

232
00:16:14.250 --> 00:16:16.190
Such a nuisance...

233
00:16:17.690 --> 00:16:20.090
We'll just have to kill them all.

234
00:16:22.790 --> 00:16:25.950
Yeah, I'm starting to feel like I can do this!

235
00:16:25.950 --> 00:16:39.460
Buggy! Buggy!

236
00:16:39.460 --> 00:16:41.810
Be silent, you brazen idiots!

237
00:16:42.340 --> 00:16:45.720
You're letting your emotions run away with you.

238
00:16:45.720 --> 00:16:48.030
This ship won't stop!

239
00:16:48.030 --> 00:16:50.270
It's headed straight for the battlefield!

240
00:16:50.270 --> 00:16:53.680
And we're all on board.

241
00:16:53.680 --> 00:16:55.680
Just think about it!

242
00:16:56.270 --> 00:17:01.900
We're within arm's reach of the summit,
where the best of the best are!

243
00:17:01.900 --> 00:17:05.390
We won't get another chance like this again in our lifetimes.

244
00:17:06.360 --> 00:17:10.300
If you're real men, won't you come with me and fulfill your dreams?

245
00:17:10.300 --> 00:17:16.250
Today, I will take Whitebeard's head, and with it, the whole world!

246
00:17:16.250 --> 00:17:18.920
Yeah! Captain Buggy!

247
00:17:25.330 --> 00:17:27.490
Captain Buggy!

248
00:17:28.720 --> 00:17:32.000
We were plunged into the darkest depths of hell.

249
00:17:32.000 --> 00:17:36.530
At some point, we lost something important!

250
00:17:36.530 --> 00:17:40.940
We used to have it! That inner gem known as dreams!

251
00:17:40.940 --> 00:17:43.620
We'll follow you to the ends of the world!

252
00:17:43.620 --> 00:17:45.860
Who needs a peaceful life anyway?!

253
00:17:47.890 --> 00:17:51.270
That's right! Let's go, men!

254
00:17:51.270 --> 00:17:53.620
To Navy HQ!

255
00:17:56.540 --> 00:18:12.750
Buggy! Buggy!

256
00:17:56.540 --> 00:17:58.560
Looks like they've come to an agreement.

257
00:17:58.560 --> 00:18:01.290
He seems to have a talent for convincing people, at least.

258
00:18:01.290 --> 00:18:04.860
Captain Buggy, you're one of the world's real trailblazers!

259
00:18:04.860 --> 00:18:07.470
We'll follow you anywhere!

260
00:18:08.750 --> 00:18:10.870
Go ahead and follow me!

261
00:18:12.750 --> 00:18:14.920
Just do whatever vyou want.

262
00:18:21.450 --> 00:18:24.920
On the same island as Navy HQ, Marineford,

263
00:18:24.920 --> 00:18:29.650
there is a large town where mainly the marines' families reside.

264
00:18:37.730 --> 00:18:42.920
All those citizens have been ordered to evacuate.

265
00:18:47.330 --> 00:18:55.050
From their new haven in Sabaody Archipelago,
the people eagerly watch the execution via monitors.

266
00:18:59.620 --> 00:19:02.680
Reporters and cameramen have
 gathered from all over the world

267
00:19:02.680 --> 00:19:07.660
to watch and keep the rest of the world informed.

268
00:19:08.910 --> 00:19:12.690
Navy HQ has put all their forces into this.

269
00:19:12.690 --> 00:19:16.150
Of course. And I'm sure Whitebeard knows.

270
00:19:16.800 --> 00:19:19.670
So, will he really show?

271
00:19:20.890 --> 00:19:26.150
All scouting ships dispatched by the Navy have been sunk.

272
00:19:26.820 --> 00:19:29.730
Nobody has seen any trace of Whitebeard,

273
00:19:30.480 --> 00:19:34.330
and the tension at Marineford keeps building.

274
00:19:37.200 --> 00:19:42.780
Less than three hours remain before the execution.

275
00:20:10.050 --> 00:20:11.140
Go up the stairs.

276
00:20:32.920 --> 00:20:35.210
Listen, Luffy!

277
00:20:35.910 --> 00:20:40.690
We have to live our lives without regrets!

278
00:20:40.690 --> 00:20:42.220
Yeah!

279
00:21:05.120 --> 00:21:07.650
Someday, we'll head out to sea,

280
00:21:07.650 --> 00:21:09.850
and then we'll be able to do whatever we want!

281
00:21:12.910 --> 00:21:14.710
No one will have more freedom than us!

282
00:21:35.380 --> 00:21:39.780
<b>The South Blue</b>

283
00:21:40.950 --> 00:21:44.810
Three hours to go. I wonder if
 Whitebeard's already shown himself?

284
00:21:44.810 --> 00:21:48.020
Who knows. Are you sure he'll show?

285
00:21:48.270 --> 00:21:51.320
Even if this is Whitebeard,
 he's gotten pretty old by now, right?

286
00:21:52.510 --> 00:21:54.290
You think?

287
00:21:54.290 --> 00:21:57.630
He's a relic from before the Great Pirate Era.

288
00:21:57.630 --> 00:21:59.920
He's probably gone senile by now.

289
00:21:59.920 --> 00:22:03.630
He's been quiet these last few years.

290
00:22:04.660 --> 00:22:09.710
<b>The East Blue</b>

291
00:22:10.420 --> 00:22:13.130
He's been around for ages.

292
00:22:13.850 --> 00:22:17.180
Can the Navy high command be defeated?

293
00:22:17.180 --> 00:22:21.810
Regardless of who wins,
 there's going to be heavy casualties.

294
00:22:25.290 --> 00:22:31.930
It'd be best if he didn't show,
and the execution went ahead without incident.

295
00:22:32.650 --> 00:22:35.830
<b>The North Blue</b>

296
00:22:38.730 --> 00:22:42.140
Hey! Hey! I want some booze, old man!

297
00:22:42.140 --> 00:22:44.850
You think I'm gonna open the pub on a day like this?!

298
00:22:44.850 --> 00:22:47.790
War might break out, you know!

299
00:22:47.790 --> 00:22:51.580
Go home! If the world's still here tomorrow, I'll open the pub then!

300
00:22:51.580 --> 00:22:53.980
Then please, just sell me some booze!

301
00:22:53.980 --> 00:22:57.390
It feels like we're the ones facing execution here!

302
00:22:57.390 --> 00:23:00.170
We gotta have a drink to endure this!

303
00:23:01.390 --> 00:23:06.500
Don't think of him as just some old guy; he's as strong as ever.

304
00:23:02.840 --> 00:23:06.500
<b>The West Blue</b>

305
00:23:06.500 --> 00:23:13.870
We saw him a year ago, and he was just sitting there.

306
00:23:19.230 --> 00:23:21.110
We lost all hope that we would survive.

307
00:23:21.860 --> 00:23:25.780
<b>The Grand Line</b>

308
00:23:22.440 --> 00:23:25.780
Is Whitebeard really such a terrifying pirate?

309
00:23:26.750 --> 00:23:28.700
Even the kids know.

310
00:23:28.700 --> 00:23:30.620
They're singing about him while jumping rope.

311
00:23:30.620 --> 00:23:35.490
♪ The pirate, Whitebeard, scarier than the devil! ♪

312
00:23:36.010 --> 00:23:37.850
Dear Lord,

313
00:23:38.500 --> 00:23:42.870
where is this world headed?

314
00:23:51.740 --> 00:23:55.450
<b>Navy Headquarters
Marineford, The Grand Line</b>

315
00:24:01.220 --> 00:24:02.810
Hurry and get ready!

316
00:24:02.810 --> 00:24:04.460
You! Move it!

317
00:24:13.230 --> 00:24:15.480
Show no fear!

318
00:24:15.480 --> 00:24:18.440
Whatever happens, only three hours remain.

319
00:24:19.800 --> 00:24:22.140
Then all of this will be over!

320
00:24:27.780 --> 00:24:34.020
In all, more than 100,000 marines
 have gathered from all over the world.

321
00:24:36.160 --> 00:24:41.560
Fifty battleships encircle the crescent-shaped bay.

322
00:24:42.040 --> 00:24:45.960
And within the bay, countless cannons are ready.

323
00:24:47.120 --> 00:24:51.340
The front row of the troops
 can be seen from the port.

324
00:24:54.060 --> 00:24:57.200
Among them are the five rogues that could decide the outcome of this war,

325
00:24:57.200 --> 00:24:59.780
the members of the Seven Warlords of the Sea.

326
00:25:00.590 --> 00:25:06.950
Below the execution platform, Navy HQ's most powerful combat force stands guard:

327
00:25:07.340 --> 00:25:10.590
the three Navy admirals!

328
00:25:14.480 --> 00:25:17.480
<b>Navy Admiral
“Aokiji” Kuzan</b>

329
00:25:18.950 --> 00:25:21.920
<b>Navy Admiral
“Akainu” Sakazuki</b>

330
00:25:23.330 --> 00:25:26.300
<b>Navy Admiral
“Kizaru” Borsalino</b>

331
00:25:29.960 --> 00:25:31.210
Now,

332
00:25:31.210 --> 00:25:34.470
all the world's forces of justice...

333
00:25:34.470 --> 00:25:37.100
await the Whitebeard Pirates...

334
00:25:37.100 --> 00:25:40.410
to prevent them from rescuing Ace.

335
00:25:58.440 --> 00:26:00.060
I see it!

336
00:26:00.060 --> 00:26:02.870
Hey! Jinbe!

337
00:26:02.870 --> 00:26:06.070
I can see the Gate of Justice!

338
00:26:06.070 --> 00:26:07.410
That was fast!

339
00:26:07.410 --> 00:26:09.400
No, we're actually pretty late!

340
00:26:09.400 --> 00:26:12.480
If the wind had been more favorable, we would have arrived sooner!

341
00:26:14.140 --> 00:26:17.690
So, how are we going to get through that gate?

342
00:26:18.220 --> 00:26:21.490
My men! It's almost time!

343
00:26:22.270 --> 00:26:24.030
Time for what?

344
00:26:24.030 --> 00:26:27.480
Time for Captain Buggy to take over the world!

345
00:26:28.400 --> 00:26:29.930
That's right, my comrades!

346
00:26:29.930 --> 00:26:32.800
Who cares about Navy HQ?!

347
00:26:43.480 --> 00:26:46.850
Hey, look! There's Fire Fist Ace!

348
00:26:50.150 --> 00:26:57.530
That's the man that could trigger this world-changing war!

349
00:27:01.130 --> 00:27:06.540
The fate of the world depends on him!

350
00:27:33.200 --> 00:27:36.510
I'm gonna tell them everything, Garp.

351
00:27:36.510 --> 00:27:39.940
Do whatever you want. I'll be down there.

352
00:27:46.100 --> 00:27:47.460
Stand down.

353
00:27:47.460 --> 00:27:48.380
Yes, sir!

354
00:27:49.050 --> 00:27:50.970
Fleet Admiral Sengoku!

355
00:27:50.970 --> 00:27:52.050
What's happening?

356
00:27:52.050 --> 00:27:53.720
Give me the transponder snail.

357
00:27:53.720 --> 00:27:54.860
Yes, sir.

358
00:28:03.240 --> 00:28:06.430
I have an announcement for you all.

359
00:28:11.130 --> 00:28:13.180
Portgas D. Ace...

360
00:28:13.180 --> 00:28:18.040
The execution of this man is of paramount importance.

361
00:28:19.710 --> 00:28:22.020
You've done nothing wrong.

362
00:28:24.600 --> 00:28:28.240
Women always get sympathetic at times like this, Tsuru-chan.

363
00:28:28.620 --> 00:28:32.620
Ace. What is your father's name?!

364
00:28:37.020 --> 00:28:38.010
His father?

365
00:28:38.010 --> 00:28:39.830
What's this all about?

366
00:28:42.800 --> 00:28:44.640
My father is Whitebeard.

367
00:28:44.640 --> 00:28:45.670
Not true!

368
00:28:45.670 --> 00:28:49.840
It is! Whitebeard is the only father I have!

369
00:28:50.660 --> 00:28:55.450
Years ago, we dedicated a lot of manpower to following his movements.

370
00:28:55.450 --> 00:28:59.830
We suspected that man might have conceived a child on a certain island.

371
00:28:59.830 --> 00:29:05.230
We relied entirely on Cipher Pol's vague information about this possibility.

372
00:29:05.230 --> 00:29:07.800
Newborns...

373
00:29:08.310 --> 00:29:10.760
The unborn...

374
00:29:10.760 --> 00:29:16.230
We investigated every possible infant and their mothers but we found nothing.

375
00:29:17.040 --> 00:29:18.810
But I suppose that was to be expected.

376
00:29:18.810 --> 00:29:23.020
Your mother risked her life to deliver you safely.

377
00:29:23.020 --> 00:29:26.710
She performed a special trick.

378
00:29:31.200 --> 00:29:38.030
She deceived us... 
No, she deceived the whole world!

379
00:29:38.030 --> 00:29:41.660
She lived on an island called Baterilla, in the South Blue.

380
00:29:42.880 --> 00:29:47.900
Her name was Portgas D. Rouge.

381
00:29:48.400 --> 00:29:54.840
Your mother used her sheer willpower to pull off something unimaginable.

382
00:29:54.840 --> 00:29:59.710
She carried her child in her womb for 20 whole months.

383
00:30:02.110 --> 00:30:04.110
What is he saying?

384
00:30:04.110 --> 00:30:10.290
She used all of her strength
 and died as soon as she gave birth to you.

385
00:30:13.780 --> 00:30:17.190
And so a year and three months after the father's death,

386
00:30:17.190 --> 00:30:22.250
a child was born, carrying the blood of the most evil man in the world.

387
00:30:25.660 --> 00:30:27.370
That child was you!

388
00:30:30.340 --> 00:30:33.180
I'm sure you already know...

389
00:30:40.850 --> 00:30:44.320
A newborn bears no sin.

390
00:30:44.890 --> 00:30:46.730
Garp.

391
00:30:47.480 --> 00:30:49.530
Take care of my child.

392
00:30:51.960 --> 00:30:54.800
Your father is...

393
00:30:57.680 --> 00:31:02.340
the pirate king, Gold Roger!

394
